          <ref target="#note-0000002103583228">cadence in
          the eleventh measure</ref>, a melody has to be invented in the right
          hand and to be continued for about ten measures, up to
          the subsequent
          <ref target="#note-0000000417006726">cadence to C#</ref>, approximately in the following manner:</s>   
          <notatedMusic>
            <ptr target="music-example1.xml" />
          </notatedMusic>
        </p>
      </div>

      <pb n="429" />

      <div n="3">
        <head>§. 3.</head>
        <p>
          <s corresp="comments_1731.xml#p3-1-s1">In the 19th measure<note type="editorial" resp="#pfeffer">Measure 29, with the second <hi rendition="#i">si suona</hi>, is meant; measure 19 has none.</note>, there is again a
          <ref target="#si-suona-2">si suona</ref>, of which the meaning
          is known,<note type="editorial" resp="#pfeffer">Cf. Probstück 5.</note> and where the
          <ref target="#tutti-1 #tutti-2 #tutti-3 #tutti-4">tutti</ref> enters, everything is possible <!-- ? -->
          which only sounds well.</s>
          <s corresp="comments_1731.xml#p3-1-s2"><ref target="#measure-0000000574431491">After the end of the first part</ref>,
          the right hand again begins to modulate, of which this may serve as an example:</s> 

